From ef2f949402e3763d0149cd3394338ca4298d9e7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Twilight0 <twilight0@vivaldi.net>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:36:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] nouveau,nvk,nak: Fermi bound textures and NV9039 M2MF
 copy/upload support

- Lower constant-index Fermi (< KEPLER_A) sampled textures to
  NAK_NIR_TEX_REF_TYPE_BOUND via nvk_bound_tex_map and emit BIND_TSC /
  BIND_TIC before graphics draws and compute dispatches.
- Use NV9039 (M2MF) with NVKMD_ENGINE_3D for Fermi upload_queue and
  nouveau_copy_rect_m2mf() for identity-remap Fermi image/buffer copies.
- Guard Kepler-only NVA0C0 compute init/SLM/cache-invalidate methods and
  compute-QMD meta image copies behind >= KEPLER_COMPUTE_A.

Verified on GeForce GT 555M (NVC3/GF106): offscreen linear/optimal
untextured & textured draws and vkcube --wsi wayland (101.8 FPS) pass
with zero kernel faults.

Assisted-by: LLM
